# Conservative host-TU lint. Device (.cu/.cuh) TUs are OUT OF SCOPE: clang-tidy
# here is clang 14, and NVCC's CUDA dialect (warp intrinsics, __launch_bounds__,
# cooperative-groups-adjacent syntax used across csrc/rola) is not something a
# stock clang-tidy front end parses cleanly -- see docs/build.md's Standards
# lint section for what was actually tried and what it reported. This config is
# exercised on the ONE host TU named there (csrc/rola/rola_api.cpp) via
# tools/lint/compdb.sh's compile database.
#
# The check set is deliberately narrow: bugprone (real correctness classes)
# plus a small readability set, with nothing opinionated about naming or
# braces (this codebase's own style rules -- KERNEL_STANDARDS.md, the
# comments-to-docs mandate -- already govern that, and a second, disagreeing
# style opinion here would just be noise a contributor learns to ignore).
Checks: >
  -*,
  bugprone-*,
  -bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters,
  -bugprone-exception-escape,
  readability-misleading-indentation,
  readability-redundant-declaration,
  readability-simplify-boolean-expr,
  readability-container-size-empty

WarningsAsErrors: ''
HeaderFilterRegex: ''
FormatStyle: none
